MODEL_OUTPUT_BEGIN bytes=483
The scenario describes a small founding population (15 British individuals) with one carrier of a recessive gene. Over time, the isolated island population grew to 240, showing a much higher frequency of the recessive allele than expected. This is a classic example of the **founder effect**, where a small group establishes a new population and carries only a subset of the original genetic diversity, leading to allele frequencies that differ from the source population.

Answer: J
